---
import { DOCS } from '../data/site';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { kilnVersion } from '../data/kiln';

const facts = [
  ['Base', 'Arch Linux'],
  ['Packages', 'pacman, official Arch repositories'],
  ['Profiles', `kiln ${kilnVersion}`],
  ['Init', 'systemd'],
  ['Boot', 'systemd-boot, GRUB or Limine; UEFI and BIOS'],
  ['Desktop', 'twmx by default; i3, Sway, Hyprland, XFCE, KDE Plasma, GNOME or none'],
  ['License', 'MIT'],
];
---
<Base title="About" description="The goals and design of Kiln Linux, a minimal distribution based on Arch Linux.">
  <PageHeader
    title="About Kiln Linux"
    lede="Kiln is Arch Linux plus four things: a live ISO profile, an installer, a set of package profiles, and the kiln tool that applies them."
  />

  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="grid gap-y-10 pt-4 md:grid-cols-12 md:gap-x-10">
      <aside class="md:col-span-3 md:row-start-1" aria-labelledby="facts">
        <h2 id="facts" class="text-sm font-medium text-heading">At a glance</h2>
        <dl class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm">
          {facts.map(([k, v]) => <div><dt class="text-mute">{k}</dt><dd class="text-heading">{v}</dd></div>)}
        </dl>
      </aside>

      <article class="prose-k md:col-span-9 md:row-start-1 [&>h2:first-child]:mt-0">
        <h2>Goals</h2>
        <p>
          A small, readable Arch system you can install in a few minutes. Nothing replaces pacman, systemd or the Arch
          repositories. An installed Kiln system is an Arch system with a different <code>os-release</code>, some
          defaults, and <code>kiln</code>.
        </p>

        <h2>Design</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>pacman is the only package database.</strong> kiln asks pacman everything and never reads
          <code>/var/lib/pacman</code> itself. Its own state is one small file, <code>/var/lib/kiln/state.toml</code>,
          listing active profiles and the packages kiln installed for each.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>kiln never removes what you installed.</strong> Packages already present when you apply a profile
          aren’t recorded, so <code>kiln remove --purge</code> can’t touch them.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>No partial upgrades.</strong> kiln never runs <code>pacman -Sy</code>. Update with
          <code>pacman -Syu</code>, as on any Arch system.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>The installer shows its work.</strong> <code>kiln-install</code> is a bash script calling
          <code>sfdisk</code>, <code>pacstrap</code>, <code>genfstab</code>, <code>arch-chroot</code> and
          <code>bootctl</code> directly, so you can read exactly what it does.
        </p>

        <h2>Status</h2>
        <p>
          The ISO builds rootless with archiso and <code>make test</code> passes. The installer and desktop haven’t been
          run end to end in a VM yet. The <a href={`${DOCS}/status/`}>status page</a> lists what works.
        </p>

        <h2>Contributing</h2>
        <p>
          Testing installs in QEMU or on real hardware helps most right now. Start with the
          <a href={`${DOCS}/contributing/`}>contributing guide</a>.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
